+/*
+ * Exposure bias applied in the luminance estimator. The mean-based AGC
+ * meters the whole frame, so backlit scenes (bright window behind a dark
+ * subject) leave the subject heavily underexposed. Dividing the estimated
+ * luminance by this factor makes the solver raise exposure accordingly
+ * (+1 EV per factor of 2). The default constraint is a lower bound only,
+ * so it can never cancel the bias back out.
+ */
+static constexpr double kExposureBias = 2.0;
+
+/*
+ * Center-weighted metering. The luminance estimator weights each statistics
+ * cell by a Gaussian of its distance from the frame center (sigma in units
+ * of half-frame dimensions, so 1.0 reaches the edge midpoints and ~1.4 the
+ * corners). The sigma below is aggressive: the centre of the frame carries
+ * most of the meter weight and bright background objects at the frame edge
+ * contribute very little, so backlit scenes expose for the subject rather
+ * than for the window behind it. A uniformly bright scene still meters to
+ * the same value as before, so kExposureBias keeps its meaning.
+ */
+static constexpr double kCenterWeightSigma = 0.28;
+
 /* \todo Honour the FrameDurationLimits control instead of hardcoding a limit */
 static constexpr utils::Duration kMaxExposureTime = 60ms;
 
